{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02441",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 5.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Right, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.22,
      "end_seconds": 11.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.99,
      "end_seconds": 21.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "Honestly, it's a shaky feeling in my hands, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.82,
      "end_seconds": 27.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Right, how long has it it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.23,
      "end_seconds": 32.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "It's been like this since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.37,
      "end_seconds": 43.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.8,
      "end_seconds": 52.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "It feels severe to me. Stress and caffeine definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.25,
      "end_seconds": 57.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.74,
      "end_seconds": 69.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "It usually comes with sweaty palms. The sweaty palms? That's been for about three months. As for sweaty palms, it feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.37,
      "end_seconds": 82.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.6,
      "end_seconds": 93.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. My partner and our baby. I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.5,
      "end_seconds": 98.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.21,
      "end_seconds": 105.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Grass pollen i come out in... well, itchy eyes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.45,
      "end_seconds": 109.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.9,
      "end_seconds": 111.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Nothing regular, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.71,
      "end_seconds": 120.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.75,
      "end_seconds": 124.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.57,
      "end_seconds": 129.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.77,
      "end_seconds": 132.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "no, nothing at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.0,
      "end_seconds": 145.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Any fainting, weight loss, weakness or palpitations at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.55,
      "end_seconds": 153.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "So, I haven't had fainting, weight loss, weakness or palpitations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.62,
      "end_seconds": 157.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.89,
      "end_seconds": 160.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.44,
      "end_seconds": 165.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.34,
      "end_seconds": 169.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.81,
      "end_seconds": 177.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.9,
      "end_seconds": 192.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.44,
      "end_seconds": 221.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 128 over 79, temperature is 37.0 degrees, height 157 centimetres, weight 75 kilos, heart rate 66."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.04,
      "end_seconds": 227.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.43,
      "end_seconds": 230.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.69,
      "end_seconds": 246.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "There is a fine, fast tremor that goes away when the hands are resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.65,
      "end_seconds": 254.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.41,
      "end_seconds": 279.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. I don't have a clear answer today: an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor is possible, and so is an overactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.95,
      "end_seconds": 283.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.39,
      "end_seconds": 309.71,
      "duration_seconds": 22.32,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor do well once it's treated properly. Let's get a thyroid test, for tremor. Cut down caffeine and try slow breathing when it starts. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.83,
      "end_seconds": 312.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "That's fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.11,
      "end_seconds": 317.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.09,
      "end_seconds": 321.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}